# /etc/dyai/credentials/ana-dashboard/dashboard_env — root:root 600. Example only: real values never enter Git.
# ANA_ACCESS_MODE, ANA_CONTAINER, HOSTNAME and PORT are pinned in dyai-ana-dashboard.service; values here cannot override them.
CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com
CF_ACCESS_AUD=<64-hex AUD tag of the ana.dyai.cloud Access application>
ANA_ALLOWED_EMAILS=<exactly the three invited addresses of the Access policy, comma-separated>
SOCIAL_IG_WORKER_URL=https://login.dyai.cloud
SOCIAL_IG_INTERNAL_READ_KEY=<the worker's INTERNAL_READ_KEY>
# Jira: unset = the views show "not configured". Which account the server uses is an owner decision (ANA-33).
# JIRA_BASE_URL=https://dyai2026.atlassian.net
# JIRA_EMAIL=<integration account>
# JIRA_API_TOKEN=<its API token>
# ANA Brain projection (ANA-35, deploy/ana-brain): the Brain runs on this host on loopback. The token is issued with
# `brain.sh issue-dashboard-token` on the host; unset = the Brain page shows "not configured".
# BRAIN_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8790
# BRAIN_API_TOKEN=<the dashboard token of the Brain>
# ANA World "Was läuft": once a day a digest into the Brain as agent:lumen (brain.sh issue-key agent:lumen); loopback only
# ANA_BRAIN_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8790/mcp
# ANA_BRAIN_WRITE_KEY=<the agent key>
# ANA World (ANA-48): Ana's current region for the 3D world, region level only, never committed. Unset = "place not set".
# An optional fourth field is the IANA time zone of the place (her clock and when she sleeps); without it the local time
# is estimated from the longitude.
# WORLD_ANA_PLACE=<label>;<lat>;<lon>[;<time zone, e.g. Europe/Lisbon>]
# ANA World looks (ANA-48): a Claude vision model reads the cover image of Ana's newest post for her look and outfit
# colours (on Ana's request). Only that image is sent, never a caption. Unset = looks from captions and hand picks only.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<key>
# WORLD_VISION_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
#
# World analyst (Jira ANAK-3). Unset WORLD_ANALYST_PROVIDER means off: no provider, worker or Brain call. Switching it on
# sends the question, per-post metrics and categories, group medians and released Brain segments to the chosen provider, so it
# needs a provider, privacy and cost approval first.
# Each provider has its own variable; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above is never read here. There is no fallback between providers.
# First provider to switch on: anthropic with WORLD_ANALYST_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5. No new key is needed for it: whoever may
# change this file on the host can give WORLD_ANALYST_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY the same value as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Then the analyst
# shares one account's spend and rate limits with everything else on that key: looks, post categories, office topics,
# newsletters and the brief. WORLD_ANALYST_DAILY_CAP limits only the analyst.
# WORLD_ANALYST_PROVIDER=anthropic|openai|openrouter
# WORLD_ANALYST_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<key>
# WORLD_ANALYST_OPENAI_API_KEY=<key>
# WORLD_ANALYST_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=<key>
# WORLD_ANALYST_MODEL=<model id; required, there is no default>
# WORLD_ANALYST_DAILY_CAP=30
# Brain notes reach a provider only when their sources are listed for exactly that provider (comma list). Unset: no note text.
# WORLD_ANALYST_BRAIN_SOURCES_ANTHROPIC=
# WORLD_ANALYST_BRAIN_SOURCES_OPENAI=
# WORLD_ANALYST_BRAIN_SOURCES_OPENROUTER=

# Office Berlin: who is who on the board (role:email, comma separated). Without it nobody can use the board.
# OFFICE_PEOPLE=ana:<email>,ben:<email>,vince:<email>
